    "explanation": "Zeratul is at his best when there are plenty of opportunities to roam and gank. Maps that split the attention of the opposing team with multiple Objective spawns or reasons to rotate give him such opportunities. Conversely, Maps with an emphasis on grouping up, laning and waveclearing suit him poorly.\n\nZeratul is very dependent on his Level 16 Talents, and therefore, does not do well on snowball maps, like Tomb of the Spider Queen or Braxis Holdout."
